<InformationLayout title="Terms of Use" description="Educational-use guidance, chemistry model limitations, local progress backups, and the Elementa source-code license.">
  <p>Last updated November 11, 2026.</p>
  <h2>Educational use</h2>
  <p>
    Elementa is a free study aid for learning the periodic table. It isn't a
    substitute for a textbook, laboratory manual, teacher or official exam
    materials. Confirm values that matter for an assignment, experiment or safety
    decision against a primary reference.
  </p>
  <h2>Reference data and teaching models</h2>
  <p>
    Element pages compile published reference information and link to sources.
    Values are reference data, rather than certified measurements. Missing or
    experimentally unestablished properties may be unavailable. Simplified shell
    and subshell diagrams don't depict electron paths or scale-accurate atoms.
    A quiz score reflects that practice round; it isn't a qualification or an
    independent assessment of course mastery.
  </p>
  <h2>Progress and backups</h2>
  <p>
    Study progress is stored in your browser on your device. Use
    <a href="/study/#/saved">Export JSON on the Saved page</a> before clearing
    browser data or changing devices. Smolk Apps can't recover progress that was
    cleared or lost from your device.
  </p>
